  "notes": "Built from the archived 2025-26 bulletin's own Suggested Academic Plan and Program Requirements tabs (raw HTML tables, same DOM-extraction approach used for the 2026 build). Confirmed functionally identical to the 2026-27 catalog (this app's ARTH-2026.json) -- the 8-semester course sequence, semester-by-semester credit loads (16/16/16/15/15/15/15/12 = 120 total), every specific course placement, the Additional Courses approved list (ARTH 100, 105N, 107N, 111, 111U, 112, 112U, 120, 130, 140, 201, 202N -- no Linked-course variants, unlike 2022-23 through 2024-25, see ARTH-2022.json/ARTH-2024.json notes), the 'World Cultures'/'World Language' terminology, and the IL/US B.A. Knowledge Domain placement on Semester 5/Semester 6 are all unchanged from 2026-27. Real differences found, all cosmetic and confirmed to not affect any literal course code modeled in this plan's own semester items: (1) three course titles differ from 2026-27's wording -- ARTH 140 'Art of the Mayas, Aztecs, and Incas' (2026-27 retitles it 'Introduction to the Art and Architecture of the Mayas, Aztecs, and Incas'), ARTH/AMST 307N 'Introduction to American Art and Society' (2026-27 drops 'Introduction to'); (2) the geographic-distribution elective pool (the generic, unenforced 'Support Course Geographic Area'/'Support Course Art History Elective' open_elective slots in this plan) lists two more courses in its Europe/Mediterranean category than 2026-27 does -- ARTH 445 'Oceanic Art' and ARTH 313 'Northern Renaissance Art' -- neither of which is a literal course-code requirement in this schema, so no slot-level change was needed. No Additional Courses list, semester sequence, or credit-total change found between this year and 2026-27.",
